course: dictionary
lesson: 6930
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Paddle can be a thing you hold, or something you do. The context, the words around it, tells you which meaning is right. «The next week he paddles.» Here paddle is a verb, an action, so it means to move a boat with a paddle, or to walk in shallow water.
explain: «Now the Man must paddle all the way home.» The Man is in a boat, so paddle means to move the boat with a paddle. Always check: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Words also show what they are doing in a sentence. In «Rat and Mole were mending paddles», paddles is a noun, a thing, the flat wide ends of the poles that push a boat. Look for «a» or «the» and for words like «mending» or «hunting for». These clues tell you the word is a noun.
fact: A paddle can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action).
fact: As a noun, a paddle is a short pole with a flat, wide end, used to move a canoe or small boat through water.
fact: As a verb, to paddle can mean to move a boat with a paddle, or to walk in shallow water, such as at the beach.
fact: «Your dog is fast asleep on the rug, but its paws are paddling» shows paddling as a movement, like the paws moving in water.
fact: Phrases to know: paddle a canoe, go for a paddle, paddling pool, paddle steamer. In American English, a paddle can also be a bat for table tennis.
exercise: «Now the Man must paddle all the way home.» What does paddle mean here? | To walk on a sunny beach | A bat for table tennis | *To move a boat with a paddle | A short pole with a flat end, used as a noun
exercise: «Rat and Mole were mending paddles.» Is paddles a noun or a verb here? | *A noun, because it is a thing you can mend | A verb, because it is an action | A verb, because it ends in s | An adjective, because it describes the boat
exercise: «Your dog is fast asleep on the rug, but its paws are paddling.» What is happening to the paws? | They are being dried with a towel | *They are moving like paddles, in a steady back-and-forth motion | They are being washed in the bath | They are wagging quickly to say hello
test: At the beach, Ella and her cousin paddle in the shallows while Dad watches. What does paddle mean? | To steer a canoe out to sea | A flat wide pole | *To walk in shallow water | A table tennis bat
test: Grandma bought a new paddle for the canoe. What kind of word is paddle here? | A verb, because it is in the past tense | *A noun, because it is a thing | A verb, because it is an action | An adjective, because it describes the canoe
exam: Which sentence uses paddle as a verb that means to walk in shallow water? | *The children paddle in the stream while the adult watches | Dad hung the paddle on the wall | The canoe has a new paddle | The table tennis paddle was cracked
